<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Intef I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 2134–2117 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/22nd-century-bce">22nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Intef I was a ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a> in the late 22nd century BCE, the first of the Eleventh Dynasty to claim the full titles of a king. Building on the position of his predecessor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mentuhotep-i">Mentuhotep I</a>, he asserted royal authority over the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nome">nomes</a> in rivalry with the Herakleopolitan kings of the north. He was buried in a rock-cut saff tomb at el-Tarif on the west bank of Thebes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/intef-i.jpg" alt="Intef I" width="320" height="287" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan R. Lazaro · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Intef_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
